  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(406.27pt, 481.15pt, "), we can pinpoint the Mie ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 495.79pt, "transition bottleneck where structural complexity reaches its global maximum. This metric allows ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 510.43pt, "us to contrast the \"physical entropy\" inherent in the scattering manifold against the \"spurious ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 525.07pt, "entropy\" introduced by the FFT’s periodic boundary mismatch. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 15.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0f4761"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 551.35pt, "Manifold Compression and Fidelity Scaling ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 571.27pt, "To evaluate the compressibility of the extinction manifold and the efficiency of the harmonic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 585.91pt, "bases, we employed two complementary truncation strategies. These methods were designed to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 600.58pt, "characterize the minimum degrees of freedom required for physical representation and the rate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 615.22pt, "of information decay under hardware constraints. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 14.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0f4761"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 639.7pt, "Cumulative Energy Thresholding (The Sparsity Metric) ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 658.9pt, "This approach identifies the intrinsic cardinality of the ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(342.91pt, 658.9pt, "𝑄")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.52pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(350.71pt, 661.3pt, "𝑒𝑥𝑡")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(364.75pt, 658.9pt, " signal by determining the absolute ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 673.54pt, "minimum number of basis functions needed to represent the physics. For both the DCT and FFT, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 688.3pt, "we calculated the normalized power of every coefficient, sorted them in descending order of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 702.936pt, "magnitude, and summed them cumulatively. ")
